  "forensic_findings": {
    "1_statistical_breakthrough_8shot": "Fixed-control subset s*=[13, 15, 22] achieved a statistically significant +14.00 pp improvement (32.00% -> 46.00%) over baseline with McNemar p=5.19e-4 and Holm-Bonferroni corrected p=0.0021. Contingency table b=15, c=1 proves 15 previously failed questions were solved with only 1 regression.",
    "2_cooperative_synergy": "S5 calibration evidence confirms multi-layer cooperative synergy: single layers K=1 showed poor NLL (1.021-1.029), pairs K=2 reached (1.013-1.020), while triples K=3 dominated (1.008-1.010), with [13, 15, 22] achieving 47% greedy calibration accuracy.",
    "3_router_underrouting_collapse": "Router distillation in S2 collapsed to K=2 ({13, 22}) on 100% of 4-shot and 8-shot prompts, dropping Layer 15. While {13, 22} alone produced +7.00 pp (39.00%, p=0.039), it missed the additional +7.00 pp provided by Layer 15 in the triple.",
    "4_gate_passthrough_fallback": "Token gate was demoted to passthrough (alpha=1.0) during S5 calibration due to an exact accuracy tie (45% vs 45%) and marginal NLL increase (+0.000166). In Raw ARS where gate was forced active, it achieved top performance in 4-shot (48% lenient) but matched router-only at 39% in 8-shot.",
